# UI-STD-004 — Server Action Refresh Pattern

After a successful Server Action:

1. **Update the affected UI using returned data** — e.g. `setPanel(result.data)` or `setParty(result.data)`.
2. **Use `revalidatePath()` on the server** in the action so the next navigation or hard reload is fresh.
3. **Do NOT call `router.refresh()` inside `useTransition()`** — it keeps `isPending` true until a slow full RSC reload completes.
4. **Use `router.refresh()` only when no returned data can reasonably update the UI** (rare; document why).
5. **Prefer shared workspace state over full-page refreshes** for cross-panel synchronization.

## Example — workspace tab panel

```tsx
function applyPanelResult(result: PanelActionResult, successMessage: string) {
  if (!result.success) {
    setError(result.error.message);
    return;
  }
  setError(null);
  setMessage(successMessage);
  setPanel(result.data);
}

startTransition(async () => {
  const result = await updateSomethingAction(partyId, payload);
  applyPanelResult(result, "Saved.");
});
```

## Example — server action

```ts
const data = await service.update(context, partyId, payload);
revalidatePath(`/parties/${partyId}`);
return { success: true, data };
```

## Anti-pattern

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — races the transition; "Saving…" hangs until RSC reload finishes
startTransition(async () => {
  const result = await saveAction(...);
  if (result.success) {
    router.refresh();
  }
});
```
